   "id": "b96abf55",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Bring your own region: full pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook walks the four-source CoDiT pipeline end-to-end for a region\n",
    "and date range you choose. It downloads raw NetCDFs (Global Drifter Program,\n",
    "HYCOM, ERA5, Copernicus/GLORYS), preprocesses them into a merged training h5,\n",
    "trains a small CoDiT-GRU on the result, and evaluates on one held-out patch.\n",
    "\n",
    "Prerequisites:\n",
    "- `CODIT_DATA_PATH` set to a writeable directory (bathymetry files preinstalled\n",
    "  under `$CODIT_DATA_PATH/bathymetry/` — see `scripts/download_data.py --bathymetry`).\n",
    "- `config.ini` populated with Copernicus and CDS credentials (see project README).\n",
    "\n",
    "See `docs/data_format.md` for the processed-data schema."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "fb4059ca",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "from datetime import datetime, timedelta\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "import jax\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "from jax import numpy as jnp\n",
    "\n",
    "from codit.data_module import config_funcs, config_paths, dataset_download\n",
    "from codit.data_module.dataset import OceanDataset, OceanTrainingDataset\n",
    "from codit.data_module.preprocessing import preprocess_configs\n",
    "from codit.model_module.diffusion_model import CoDiTModel\n",
    "from codit.eval_module.eval_runner import run_eval\n",
    "\n",
    "np.random.seed(0)\n",
    "key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ab4932b9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Choose a region, date range, and split policy\n",
    "\n",
    "Edit the values below. `train/val/test` splits are date-based: pick three\n",
    "non-overlapping windows inside your chosen date range.\n",
    "\n",
    "For a quick smoke run, keep the region small (≤2° square). Drifter data is\n",
    "sparse: NOAA ERDDAP returns HTTP 404 when no drifter passes through the bbox\n",
    "during the requested window. If your test split downloads no drifters,\n",
    "widen its date range (≥2 weeks recommended) or enlarge the bbox."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b24b9235",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "DATASET_NAME = 'my_region'\n",
    "CENTER_LAT, CENTER_LON = 24.0, -89.5  # Gulf of Mexico (roughly centred)\n",
    "COORD_DELTA = 8.5                     # bbox half-width in degrees — covers the full Gulf\n",
    "CONTEXT_DELTA = 0.5                   # extra degrees around bbox for context\n",
    "\n",
    "# val must yield >=128 snippets (val_dataloader batch_size is hardcoded in\n",
    "# diffusion_model.py); ~3 snippets/day at this bbox → ~45 days of val.\n",
    "SPLITS = {\n",
