    "\n",
    "PREDICTION_LENGTH = 24  # keep short for quick BYOR runs\n",
    "NUM_GRID_POINTS = 16\n",
    "DELTA_METRES = 10000"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9352cc92",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Build one config per split, download raw data\n",
    "\n",
    "Each split gets a single patch YAML. If you want multiple patches per split,\n",
    "loop over sub-regions and produce one config per sub-region."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "b92ab765",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "min_lat = CENTER_LAT - COORD_DELTA\n",
    "max_lat = CENTER_LAT + COORD_DELTA\n",
    "min_lon = CENTER_LON - COORD_DELTA\n",
    "max_lon = CENTER_LON + COORD_DELTA\n",
    "\n",
    "split_configs = {}\n",
    "for split, (start_s, end_s) in SPLITS.items():\n",
    "    start = datetime.strptime(start_s, '%Y-%m-%d')\n",
    "    end = datetime.strptime(end_s, '%Y-%m-%d')\n",
    "    cfg_dir = os.path.join(config_paths.CONFIG_PATH, DATASET_NAME, split)\n",
    "    os.makedirs(cfg_dir, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "    raw = {\n",
    "        'name': f'{DATASET_NAME}_{split}',\n",
    "        'latitudes': [min_lat, max_lat],\n",
    "        'longitudes': [min_lon, max_lon],\n",
    "        'start_date': start,\n",
    "        'end_date': end,\n",
    "        'context_delta': CONTEXT_DELTA,\n",
    "        'description': f'{DATASET_NAME} {split} split',\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    config_funcs.save_config(raw, cfg_dir, config_paths.DATA_PATH)\n",
    "    cfg = config_funcs.load_config(raw['name'], cfg_dir)\n",
    "    split_configs[split] = cfg\n",
    "list(split_configs)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "df1ed609",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Download raw NetCDFs per split. Each download populates the config's\n",
    "# dataset_path with hycom/, era5/, copernicus/, trajectories/ subdirs.\n",
    "# Comment out sources you already have on disk.\n",
    "for split, cfg in split_configs.items():\n",
    "    print(f'--- downloading {split} ---')\n",
    "    dataset_download.download_drifter(cfg)\n",
    "    dataset_download.download_hycom(cfg)\n",
    "    dataset_download.download_era5(cfg)\n",
    "    dataset_download.download_copernicus(cfg)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3c0d29aa",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Preprocess each split into a merged training h5\n",
    "\n",
    "`preprocess_configs` builds one intermediate h5 per patch (cached under\n",
    "the patch's `dataset_path`) and merges them into `output_path`. If you\n",
    "re-run this cell it re-uses the cached intermediates."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "de993466",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import xarray as xr, numpy as np                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  \n",
    "cfg = split_configs['test']                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      \n",
    "ds = xr.open_dataset(cfg['trajectories_file'])                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \n",
    "print(f\"total rows: {len(ds.time)}\")                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \n",
    "print(f\"unique drifters: {len(np.unique(ds.ID.values))}\")                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         \n",
    "# for each drifter, longest run of strictly hourly consecutive observations\n",
    "import pandas as pd                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               \n",
    "df = pd.DataFrame({'ID': ds.ID.values, 'time': ds.time.values}).sort_values(['ID','time'])\n",
    "runs = []                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         \n",
    "for name, g in df.groupby('ID'):\n",
    "    diffs = np.diff(g['time'].values).astype('timedelta64[s]').astype(int)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \n",
    "    # split into consecutive-hourly runs                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          \n",
    "    breaks = np.where(diffs != 3600)[0]                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           \n",
    "    starts = np.concatenate([[0], breaks + 1])                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \n",
    "    ends = np.concatenate([breaks + 1, [len(g)]])                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \n",
    "    runs.extend(ends - starts)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \n",
    "runs = np.asarray(runs)\n",
    "print(f\"run-length stats: max={runs.max()}, median={int(np.median(runs))}, \"                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      \n",
    "    f\"# runs >=25h: {(runs >= 25).sum()}\")       "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1d9e2030",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "processed_paths = {}\n",
    "for split, cfg in split_configs.items():\n",
    "    out = os.path.join(config_paths.DATA_PATH, 'datasets', DATASET_NAME, split, 'processed')\n",
    "    result = preprocess_configs(\n",
    "        configs=[cfg],\n",
    "        length=PREDICTION_LENGTH,\n",
    "        num_grid_points=NUM_GRID_POINTS,\n",
    "        delta_metres=DELTA_METRES,\n",
    "        output_path=out,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    processed_paths[split] = result\n",
    "processed_paths"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "22502ad6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Load train/val and fit CoDiT-GRU"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "0ae99a14",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "train_ds = OceanTrainingDataset.from_disk(\n",
    "    os.path.join(config_paths.DATA_PATH, 'datasets', DATASET_NAME, 'train', 'processed'),\n",
    "    PREDICTION_LENGTH,\n",
    ")\n",
    "val_ds = OceanTrainingDataset.from_disk(\n",
    "    os.path.join(config_paths.DATA_PATH, 'datasets', DATASET_NAME, 'val', 'processed'),\n",
    "    PREDICTION_LENGTH,\n",
    ")\n",
    "train_ds.remove_nans()\n",
    "val_ds.remove_nans()\n",
    "train_ds.load_into_memory()\n",
    "val_ds.load_into_memory()\n",
    "len(train_ds), len(val_ds)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3f221162",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "model = CoDiTModel(\n",
    "    name=f'codit_GRU_{DATASET_NAME}',\n",
    "    params={\n",
    "        'prediction_length': PREDICTION_LENGTH,\n",
    "        'dt': 1.0 / PREDICTION_LENGTH,\n",
    "        'model_type': 'GRU',\n",
    "        'context_encoder_type': 'conv',\n",
    "        'K': 20,\n",
    "        'vars': ['hycom_current', 'copernicus_current', 'era5_wind', 'bathymetry'],\n",
    "    },\n",
    ")\n",
    "model.fit(\n",
    "    train_ds,\n",
    "    val_ds,\n",
    "    train_params={\n",
    "        'num_epochs': 10,\n",
    "        'num_batches_per_epoch': 20,\n",
    "        'batch_size': 32,\n",
    "        'val_batch_size': 64,\n",
    "        'learning_rate': 1e-3,\n",
    "        'optimizer': 'adam',\n",
    "        'force_retrain': True,\n",
    "        'early_stopping_patience': 100,\n",
    "        'early_stopping_min_delta': 1e-6,\n",
    "    },\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a195aade",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Evaluate on the held-out test patch"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "9a6d8349",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "test_cfg = split_configs['test']\n",
    "test_ds = OceanDataset(test_cfg, PREDICTION_LENGTH, NUM_GRID_POINTS, DELTA_METRES, 'linear')\n",
    "n_test = len(test_ds)\n",
    "print(f'test snippets available: {n_test}')\n",
    "if n_test == 0:\n",
    "    print('Empty test set — widen your test date range or the bounding box.')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    distances, pred_coords, true_coords = run_eval(\n",
    "        model,\n",
    "        test_ds,\n",
    "        indices=list(range(min(n_test, 3))),\n",
    "        length=PREDICTION_LENGTH,\n",
    "        num_samples=10,\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    print('mean final-step distance (m):', float(jnp.nanmean(distances[..., -1])))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "024c8250",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Next steps\n",
    "\n",
    "- Increase `K`, `num_epochs`, `batch_size`, and the geographic/temporal extent\n",
    "  to approach paper-scale results.\n",
    "- The final trained model is in-memory (`model`); persist it with\n",
    "  `model.export_trained_model('codit_GRU_' + DATASET_NAME)` to reuse in\n",
    "  `codit_eval.py` — pass `--prediction_length {PREDICTION_LENGTH}` to that\n",
    "  script since the shipped default is 72.\n",
    "- See [docs/data_format.md](../docs/data_format.md) for the frozen 8-channel\n",
    "  context layout and instructions for adding new features (which is Phase 5\n",
    "  work, not Phase 4)."
   ]
  }
